From 449d4b4bb51ce84e596fac4bf3faaf1199ac2dc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <enrico.bartky@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 16:57:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] paint: render CSS box-shadow (outset + inset, blur, rounded
 inner) for block and inline boxes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

box-shadow was stored on the computed style but never painted — only text-shadow
was. Implement box-shadow:

- Outset layers paint behind the element's background (offset + spread grown box).
- Inset layers paint over the background, inside the border box, beneath the borders:
  the frame between the border box and an inner clear rectangle (border box shrunk by
  spread, offset), emitted as up to four non-overlapping strips; the clear
  rectangle's corners are rounded concentric with the border box by filling the
  corner notches as arc-sliced fills.
- Blur (outset and inset) is approximated by concentric solid fills whose cumulative
  SrcOver coverage follows the Gaussian (std-dev blur/2) CDF across the shape edge.

Hooked into all three paint paths; outset before the background, inset after it and
before the borders. Rounded boxes clip to the border radius grown by the spread.

Fixes WPT css/css-view-transitions/inline-child-with-overflow-shadow. Verified vs
Chromium goldens: sharp outset/inset exact; rounded-corner inset ~99.96%; blurred
outset ~99.75%, blurred inset ~99.88%.
---
